@startuml budget-namespace-states
' Per-namespace budget enforcement state for one ModelProvider and one period,
' as reported in status.budgetUsage[].state.
' Source of truth: docs/src/resources/modelprovider.md +
' docs/src/gateways/llm/budgets-and-rate-limits.md
!include _style.puml

state "Normal" as Normal
state "Throttled" as Throttled
state "Blocked" as Blocked

[*] --> Normal : period opens\n(daily / weekly / monthly,\nresets at midnight UTC)

Normal --> Throttled : spend crosses a degrade\npolicy atPercent: requests\nreroute to degradeTo
Normal --> Blocked : spend crosses a block policy\natPercent, or a request would\nexceed perNamespaceUSD\nor clusterUSD
Throttled --> Blocked : block threshold or\nceiling reached

Blocked --> Normal : period rollover
Throttled --> Normal : period rollover

note right of Blocked
  requests answered
  429 budget_exhausted with
  Retry-After = seconds to the
  next period reset
end note

note bottom of Normal
  warn policies emit an event and
  change no state. Spend is monotonic
  within a period, so the only way
  back is the rollover. The state is
  per (provider, namespace) and is
  display truth; enforcement reads
  each gateway replica's live counter
  plus its peers' partials (see
  Budget State Management).
end note

@enduml
